WEBVTT

00:05.830 --> 00:08.660
Huh? You haven't turned it in yet, Chloe?

00:08.660 --> 00:12.540
Wasn't the deadline for our
career planning form due a long time ago?

00:12.540 --> 00:14.500
It's not that I haven't turned it in,

00:14.500 --> 00:16.620
I did, but then I asked to do it over.

00:16.870 --> 00:20.160
I thought I wanted to go to a liberal arts college,

00:20.160 --> 00:23.620
but I suddenly started thinking that
programming might be interesting to pursue.

00:24.120 --> 00:26.750
Ooh, look at this! The troubles of youth!

00:26.750 --> 00:28.500
A young person unsure of their path!

00:28.500 --> 00:30.950
So sayeth Lord Chikuwa!

00:30.950 --> 00:33.080
Stop forcing chikuwa into conversations.

00:33.080 --> 00:35.910
You turned yours in right away, huh, Asuka-senpai?

00:35.910 --> 00:38.660
Yup! I'm the seventh generation
to run our miso shop!

00:38.660 --> 00:40.200
You want to go to medical school, right, Yu?

00:40.200 --> 00:41.330
Yeah, I guess.

00:41.660 --> 00:43.000
How about you, Nana?

00:43.000 --> 00:45.500
Gonna marry Tomoya and become
Chocolate Banana?

00:45.500 --> 00:48.250
Ugh, Yu, did you really have to go there?

00:48.250 --> 00:50.160
Nana-chan, let's get married!

00:51.000 --> 00:53.080
Starring
Tomoya
Chiba

00:51.200 --> 00:57.120
Tomoya Chiba's hit musical is
coming to Akeyuki City for five days only!

00:53.080 --> 00:59.950
Starring
Tomoya
Chiba
The Wedding of
Nanami Nanamura

00:57.120 --> 01:00.910
"The Wedding of Nanami Nanamura",
coming to Akeyuki Cultural Hall!

01:00.910 --> 01:02.910
Man, that scared me...

01:02.910 --> 01:04.870
A musical, huh...

01:05.040 --> 01:07.250
The first performance's today, too.

01:07.250 --> 01:09.040
And the theatre's right over there.

01:09.040 --> 01:12.500
Which means that right now,
Tomoya Chiba is somewhere in the vicinity.

01:12.500 --> 01:15.580
Stop! Geez, let's just go to Octave already!

01:18.910 --> 01:21.830
Ohmigosh, we get to see Tomoya soon!

01:21.830 --> 01:24.790
Tomoya

01:22.040 --> 01:24.790
I wonder if Tomoya will see me in the crowd!

01:24.790 --> 01:26.750
I'm in Tomoya hell.
Hey, wanna wait for him after the show?

01:26.750 --> 01:28.540
What in the world is going on?

01:28.540 --> 01:31.450
Looks like everyone came here before the show.

01:31.580 --> 01:35.200
Normally, this place wouldn't be crowded,
no matter what was going on.

01:35.200 --> 01:37.410
Wow, Tomoya sure is popular.

01:37.660 --> 01:39.410
Huh? Mister Manager?

01:39.700 --> 01:41.080
What happened?

01:41.080 --> 01:44.120
Oh, I just had a little fall, that's all.

01:44.290 --> 01:46.370
Is that café au lait coming out soon?

01:46.370 --> 01:48.080
Yes, it's coming!

01:48.080 --> 01:50.290
Let me get that for you, sir!

01:50.660 --> 01:53.950
Here you are! Two Café au laits!

01:53.950 --> 01:55.370
Hope you enjoy!

01:56.330 --> 01:59.200
Hey guys, let's all help out at Octave!

01:59.790 --> 02:02.830
Today, the Radio Research Society
is gonna do community service!

02:07.080 --> 02:11.830
Earphone de fusagu hiza kakaeru

02:12.290 --> 02:17.200
Sanagi no you ni busou shiteta

02:23.040 --> 02:27.910
Me wa taikutsu na machi o mitetemo

02:28.540 --> 02:33.370
Kodou wa itsudatte kogareteta sora

02:38.700 --> 02:47.040
Mada kinou no sasakure mo itamu no ni

02:49.450 --> 02:54.200
Kyou o kowasu yume o mita

02:54.200 --> 02:59.750
Kaisoku de ukashiyou to mogaite mogaite

02:59.750 --> 03:05.290
Kokoro no kabe wa soranetarium

03:05.290 --> 03:10.540
Na mo naki tobira o wananaki akeyou

03:10.540 --> 03:16.120
Ruritateha no you ni kizu o mitome kaze o aishitai

03:16.120 --> 03:21.330
Miageteru dake no sora nante iranai

03:21.330 --> 03:27.160
Koko ni iru watashi yo watashi o koete yuke

03:27.450 --> 03:32.750
Sanagi wa tokku ni mushikago kara nigeta

03:35.540 --> 03:37.950
Day 1

03:36.160 --> 03:37.950
Welcome to Octave!

03:37.950 --> 03:40.830
I've gotta recommend the roasted green tea latte!

03:40.830 --> 03:42.290
You've gotta try it!

03:42.290 --> 03:46.750
Well, I think the maple latte is really good!

03:46.950 --> 03:49.790
I mean, pretty much everything here is good.

03:49.790 --> 03:51.750
And do you seriously like Tomoya that much?

03:51.750 --> 03:55.290
One Hot coffee, one iced coffee,
one roasted green tea latte,

03:55.290 --> 03:57.950
and one ume kobucha tea comes out to 1,710 yen.

04:00.580 --> 04:03.290
My, you're pretty good.

04:04.250 --> 04:05.660
Really?

04:07.450 --> 04:10.040
What's wrong, Asuka-senpai?

04:10.330 --> 04:12.750
If we're gonna help out,
we might as well wear costumes, right?!

04:12.750 --> 04:14.040
Huh?

04:15.330 --> 04:18.040
Day 2

04:15.790 --> 04:18.040
Welcome back!

04:28.410 --> 04:31.290
Maid outfits are kinda cliché, huh?

04:31.290 --> 04:35.040
You were the one who said it was
the go-to for café costumes!

04:35.040 --> 04:37.750
Why don't we wear different ones each day, then?

04:37.750 --> 04:40.580
Sounds good.
We could do a different theme every day.

04:40.580 --> 04:43.000
Well, I know what we have to do first...

04:43.250 --> 04:45.830
Day 3

04:43.450 --> 04:45.450
Can you celebrate?

04:46.120 --> 04:48.160
Why are you girls...?

04:48.450 --> 04:50.290
Oh crap, Kitta-chan?!

04:50.620 --> 04:53.750
You're going to see
Tomoya's musical too, Kitta-sensei?!

04:53.750 --> 04:56.160
Well, actually...

04:56.540 --> 05:00.040
Oh, so your girlfriend invited you to go!

05:00.040 --> 05:01.370
How nice!

05:02.500 --> 05:05.080
I see what this is...

05:05.080 --> 05:07.370
She's trying to get him to propose.

05:07.580 --> 05:10.660
Day 4

05:08.040 --> 05:10.660
Wanna explore the frontier?

05:11.910 --> 05:13.410
What's up, Mia?

05:15.410 --> 05:18.160
My, cowboy costumes?

05:18.160 --> 05:20.370
Well, aren't you kids so cute.

05:23.080 --> 05:25.790
P-please, have a seat over here...

05:25.910 --> 05:29.620
That's the ice-cold judge
who wielded tremendous legal power.

05:29.620 --> 05:32.330
Looks like she's just a normal lady in our world.

05:32.330 --> 05:34.290
And she's a Tomoya fan to boot.

05:34.290 --> 05:35.750
What would you recommend?

05:34.870 --> 05:37.410
Wonder which one's the happiest?

05:35.750 --> 05:37.700
Th-th-the hot iced coffee!

05:38.950 --> 05:42.750
Day 5

05:39.410 --> 05:42.750
I can't believe everyone else was busy today!

05:43.450 --> 05:45.450
Let's do what we can with just us, Yu!

05:45.450 --> 05:48.700
Well, five of us was almost too many to start with...

05:49.040 --> 05:51.200
So what are we going to do for costumes?

05:51.200 --> 05:52.790
Isn't it obvious?

05:52.790 --> 05:56.120
We did wedding dresses,
then westerns, now we'll do...

05:57.290 --> 05:59.620
Summer vacation!

06:00.120 --> 06:02.370
You'll turn the café into some creepy shop.

06:02.370 --> 06:06.700
What's creepy about using our healthy bodies
to attract younger customers?!

06:06.700 --> 06:09.160
If you think that's creepy, well, then,
you're a creepy person!

06:09.330 --> 06:10.660
Yeah, uh, no.

06:10.910 --> 06:12.910
I'm just kidding anyways.

06:12.910 --> 06:15.580
I figured we'd just go back to maid outfits.

06:15.580 --> 06:19.160
Besides, when we wore those wedding dresses,
I think we almost gave the manager a stroke.

06:23.700 --> 06:25.330
Sorry, I have to take this...

06:26.160 --> 06:27.500
What is it, Dad?

06:28.250 --> 06:32.080
Huh? Well, yeah, but...

06:32.080 --> 06:36.700
but they're just going over prep for
the practice test, it doesn't matter if I skip.

06:37.700 --> 06:39.660
Yeah... Okay.

06:39.660 --> 06:41.080
I'll go...

06:42.830 --> 06:44.750
Um, Asuka...

06:44.950 --> 06:48.580
I thought you had a lotta free time this week.

06:48.950 --> 06:51.080
You skipped out on cram school?

06:51.080 --> 06:53.950
That's no good! You can't just skip that stuff!

06:54.200 --> 06:59.000
I know, I just felt like skipping this week.

06:59.000 --> 07:02.790
Wow, never thought I'd hear that from you!

07:03.040 --> 07:04.580
Right?

07:04.580 --> 07:07.790
I think she's poisoning me.

07:08.540 --> 07:12.660
That me is sooo boring!

07:13.580 --> 07:15.290
I'm really sorry.

07:15.290 --> 07:18.410
It's okay, it's okay! Good luck at cram school!

07:22.450 --> 07:24.750
I know I said that, but...

07:24.750 --> 07:27.870
If I just had one more person.

07:29.120 --> 07:32.080
Asuka, I'm back for more miso.

07:32.620 --> 07:34.330
There's one more person.

07:34.870 --> 07:35.750
Huh?

07:37.290 --> 07:39.250
H-hold on a second!

07:39.250 --> 07:41.410
Why do I have to wear this?!

07:41.620 --> 07:43.200
Oh, don't worry!

07:43.200 --> 07:45.870
All you have to do is smile and take orders,
and smile and bring orders,

07:45.870 --> 07:47.910
and smile and ring people up!

07:47.910 --> 07:49.000
Smile?!

07:49.000 --> 07:50.870
Impossible, I can't do that!

07:51.160 --> 07:54.330
Y'know, it costs money to make all that miso.

07:55.250 --> 07:59.120
C'mon, big smile! You can do it, I know you can!

07:59.120 --> 08:00.950
Off you go!

08:02.330 --> 08:05.000
A roasted green tea latte and a coffee...

08:05.410 --> 08:06.790
Of course.

08:08.410 --> 08:10.950
That employee isn't very friendly.

08:10.950 --> 08:13.410
The other girl is so much more cheerful.

08:13.410 --> 08:14.620
Are they twins?

08:14.620 --> 08:15.700
Excuse me!

08:15.910 --> 08:18.450
I'll be right there...

08:31.000 --> 08:33.370
My, that was incredible!

08:45.950 --> 08:47.250
Welcome to Octave!

08:51.870 --> 08:52.870
Here you are.

08:54.120 --> 08:56.410
Are you ready to order?

08:56.410 --> 08:58.250
Takkun, what do you want?

08:58.250 --> 08:59.870
Hmmm...

09:04.910 --> 09:07.330
Did you come to see the musical, too?

09:07.330 --> 09:12.620
Yeah! When I grow up, I wanna be
a handsome actor, just like Tomoya!

09:12.950 --> 09:14.250
Really?

09:14.580 --> 09:16.330
Well, I think you've got it in you.

09:16.620 --> 09:19.120
Really?! Am I cool?!

09:19.120 --> 09:21.620
Come on, Takkun, what do you want to order?

09:21.620 --> 09:24.830
Um, uh, this banana drink!

09:26.620 --> 09:28.540
One banana juice and a coffee.

09:28.540 --> 09:29.950
Roger that.

09:30.370 --> 09:34.790
Hey, do you know that kid in your Fragment?

09:34.790 --> 09:36.790
Yeah, I know him well.

09:37.080 --> 09:41.750
Really? Is he different at all,
like how you and I are different?

09:42.870 --> 09:45.290
Yeah, I suppose...

09:46.330 --> 09:47.580
Asuka!

09:47.580 --> 09:51.370
Yu said you needed help,
so I ditched my dad to swing by!

09:51.580 --> 09:55.580
Huh? Wow, you look so much more
mature and pretty today.

09:55.830 --> 09:58.160
Did you change your hair? Or lose some weight?

09:58.450 --> 10:00.790
No, Nana, it's me...

10:01.330 --> 10:04.910
And I'm the childish, not-pretty me.

10:05.160 --> 10:08.620
Wait, Seriouska-chan?! What, why?!

10:09.080 --> 10:10.750
Asuka-senpai!

10:10.750 --> 10:12.620
Sorry to leave you all by yourself!

10:12.830 --> 10:16.450
Huh? You look a little different today, Asuka-senpai.

10:16.450 --> 10:20.330
Yeah. Somehow, she feels
so much calmer and transparent.

10:20.330 --> 10:23.450
S-stop staring at me! It's me!

10:23.660 --> 10:25.870
Huh?! Asuka-san?!

10:27.580 --> 10:30.750
Welcome to Annie Maxda's Twilight Jukebox.

10:31.040 --> 10:33.330
Our next request comes from radio name

10:33.330 --> 10:37.160
"Waiting for my BF of Five Years
to Propose To Me Already".

10:37.160 --> 10:40.750
Are you listening up, Mister BF? She's waiting!

10:41.410 --> 10:45.580
Asuka! I got out of cram school early!

10:46.660 --> 10:49.120
Oh, hey, Yu!

10:49.410 --> 10:53.370
We don't have any customers right now,
so we're playing around with Asuka!

10:53.700 --> 10:57.330
Huh? But that's the other Asuka, right?

10:57.700 --> 10:58.830
Huh?!

11:00.080 --> 11:02.370
C'mon, the jig is up.

11:02.370 --> 11:05.290
Awww, we couldn't fool you, huh?

11:05.290 --> 11:09.120
You know, when you get a good look
at the two of you, you see the difference.

11:09.120 --> 11:12.750
This Asuka-chan's a little sexier...

11:13.910 --> 11:16.410
Well, sorry I'm not sexy!

11:16.410 --> 11:19.330
Is it because most of the time, she's so serious?

11:19.700 --> 11:21.950
She's cuter because she's not usually like this!

11:23.200 --> 11:25.910
Well, sorry I'm not very serious!

11:26.290 --> 11:29.290
I like that she's got some darker sides to her, too.

11:30.120 --> 11:33.040
Well, sorry I'm always so blindingly bright!

11:33.040 --> 11:36.040
Well, Asuka is pretty cute, I'll admit.

11:36.040 --> 11:37.160
Shut it!

11:37.450 --> 11:39.450
What are you guys doing?

11:40.250 --> 11:43.080
Well, I guess I should take the chance
to take one, too.

11:44.080 --> 11:46.330
Hey, let's all take one together!

11:57.000 --> 11:59.290
Thank you so much, you were a real help.

11:59.290 --> 12:01.950
Are you sure you don't want anything?

12:01.950 --> 12:05.870
It's totally fine! If you paid us,
it'd just turn into a part-time job.

12:05.870 --> 12:07.250
Oh, wait!

12:07.250 --> 12:10.950
If this girl ever comes back, give her
a roasted green tea latte on the house!

12:10.950 --> 12:12.830
Huh? Hey, you can't just...

12:12.830 --> 12:16.330
It's the least I can do. Come by any time.

12:16.950 --> 12:17.950
Okay...

12:19.910 --> 12:21.500
Okay, bye!

12:22.200 --> 12:23.500
See you next week.

12:23.500 --> 12:24.580
Good work today.

12:24.580 --> 12:25.950
Good night!

12:26.830 --> 12:28.410
Bye bye!

12:28.580 --> 12:29.580
See you.

12:29.950 --> 12:32.910
Tsuchimiya Miso
Miso

12:35.330 --> 12:37.410
Good, no enemies detected.

12:37.410 --> 12:38.660
Follow me!

12:39.250 --> 12:41.200
Oh, no, I'm...

12:50.290 --> 12:52.160
Mission complete!

12:52.160 --> 12:54.370
You can stop worrying now, Asuka!

12:54.580 --> 12:58.950
You could've just given me a little bit of miso.

12:58.950 --> 13:00.660
No way!

13:00.660 --> 13:02.950
Let's have dinner, then take a bath!

13:02.950 --> 13:04.290
I'll lend you underwear!

13:04.620 --> 13:07.000
I don't know when I'll be able
to get them back to you.

13:07.000 --> 13:08.750
Whenever's good!

13:08.750 --> 13:11.580
Come on, we're close enough that
stuff like that's no problem, right?

13:12.870 --> 13:14.410
I guess...

13:16.830 --> 13:18.660
Oh, she cleaned the house today.

13:19.000 --> 13:22.790
Mom always forgets to close this door.

13:42.700 --> 13:46.290
I'm gonna go get a plate for Kyo-chan again!

13:46.290 --> 13:48.200
You wait here, Asuka.

13:49.700 --> 13:52.750
Asuka-chan! I was just coming up to call you!

13:53.040 --> 13:54.000
Oh?

13:54.000 --> 13:56.290
There are two of you?

13:57.120 --> 14:01.580
Nice to meet you.
I just became friends with Asuka-san.

14:01.580 --> 14:02.950
My name is also Asuka.

14:02.950 --> 14:04.040
What?

14:04.250 --> 14:08.750
We ran into each other in town once,
and we were so surprised at how identical we looked.

14:08.750 --> 14:12.660
That's right! And when we started talking,
I found out her name was the same as mine!

14:12.660 --> 14:16.160
Talk about a coincidence, huh?
And that's how we became friends!

14:16.700 --> 14:19.450
Oh, my! How funny!

14:19.580 --> 14:24.370
Right?! So I invited her over for dinner today!
That's okay, right?

14:24.370 --> 14:28.200
Of course! But first, what's your last name, dear?

14:28.200 --> 14:28.950
Huh?

14:28.950 --> 14:31.080
My last name...

14:31.080 --> 14:32.250
Uh...

14:32.580 --> 14:34.410
Wh-what was it again?

14:34.700 --> 14:36.200
Uh...

14:36.660 --> 14:38.290
S-Siri!

14:38.290 --> 14:39.410
Huh?

14:40.080 --> 14:43.040
S-Siri. Asuka. That's me.

14:43.330 --> 14:46.290
I see, Miss Asuka Siri!

14:46.700 --> 14:48.750
Well, nice to meet you, Siri-san!

14:49.870 --> 14:51.080
Likewise.

14:53.620 --> 14:55.370
Thanks for the food!

14:55.870 --> 14:57.370
Thank you for the food.

14:57.790 --> 15:00.200
Please, eat as much as you like.

15:00.410 --> 15:02.080
O-okay...

15:06.250 --> 15:08.790
Well? How is it? Good?

15:11.700 --> 15:13.790
Yes, very...

15:14.160 --> 15:17.160
My, you skipped over the chicken
and went right for the miso konnyaku!

15:17.160 --> 15:19.250
Such mature taste for your age!

15:19.250 --> 15:21.290
Well, your miso is just so delicious...

15:21.290 --> 15:23.700
Well, don't you know how to flatter us!

15:23.700 --> 15:25.200
Isn't that right, dear?

15:25.200 --> 15:26.200
Yeah.

15:26.410 --> 15:28.700
Siri-san, have some of this, too.

15:28.700 --> 15:30.790
They're daikon leaves dressed in miso!

15:30.790 --> 15:32.950
It's my grandma's specialty!

15:32.950 --> 15:35.080
Of course, thank you.

15:40.910 --> 15:42.250
Thank you for dinner.

15:42.250 --> 15:43.580
My, already done?

15:43.580 --> 15:46.160
Yeah. There's a lot of stuff going on at the office.

15:46.160 --> 15:49.370
Are you gonna stop by the union?
I wanna come with!

15:49.620 --> 15:50.660
No.

15:50.660 --> 15:53.950
Again?! I'm the seventh generation
to take over Tsuchimiya Miso!

15:53.950 --> 15:56.120
Isn't it about time to introduce me to everyone?

15:56.410 --> 16:00.450
So you wrote "miso maker" on your school's
career planning form, then?

16:00.450 --> 16:02.290
Huh? Yeah, I did...

16:02.660 --> 16:05.540
You shouldn't have done that, not when you're
barely prepared to take on the job.

16:06.080 --> 16:08.500
Tell your teacher you want to change your answer.

16:10.080 --> 16:11.790
Have a pleasant night.

16:11.790 --> 16:13.080
I-I will...

16:13.080 --> 16:16.540
I'm not barely prepared!
What does he think he knows, huh?!

16:17.000 --> 16:20.790
He means you should take some time
to really think it over.

16:20.790 --> 16:23.910
It's not something you absolutely have to do for us.

16:23.910 --> 16:27.450
But I'm telling him that I want to...

16:30.870 --> 16:33.250
Um, can I have seconds on rice, please?

16:33.250 --> 16:34.830
And miso soup, too!

16:35.870 --> 16:38.620
Of course, let's get you a nice big bowl.

16:43.250 --> 16:45.870
Sorry for making you jump in like that.

16:45.870 --> 16:48.950
My dad's a real blockhead sometimes.

16:49.660 --> 16:50.870
Asuka...

16:51.200 --> 16:53.870
What is it, Siri Asuka?

16:54.370 --> 16:56.120
I'll drown you in that tub.

16:56.330 --> 16:59.080
I'm just kidding! So what is it?

17:00.620 --> 17:03.620
You said you wanted to make miso...

17:03.620 --> 17:05.080
Are you already set on that?

17:05.330 --> 17:08.160
Why? I mean, I love our miso.

17:08.500 --> 17:10.700
And I do, too, but...

17:10.700 --> 17:13.040
Nobody else is gonna take over
the business, you know?

17:13.040 --> 17:16.250
If I don't do it, then our miso's flavor
will be gone forever.

17:17.580 --> 17:19.370
Geez, what?!

17:19.370 --> 17:21.950
If you've got something to say,
then come out and say it!

17:21.950 --> 17:25.830
Remember the little boy I was talking to in Octave?

17:25.830 --> 17:26.830
Huh?

17:26.830 --> 17:27.830
Yeah.

17:28.450 --> 17:33.870
In my Fragment... he's not that innocent.

17:34.450 --> 17:37.660
He's always starving, always struggling...

17:38.200 --> 17:41.040
All he can think about is surviving one more day.

17:42.330 --> 17:44.950
That's how everyone is in my world.

17:45.500 --> 17:47.700
Nobody makes plans for their future.

17:48.580 --> 17:50.910
But this Fragment is different.

17:51.450 --> 17:54.080
Nothing's holding you back,
so you can dream freely.

17:54.580 --> 17:58.120
I think inheriting a miso shop is a great dream.

17:58.120 --> 18:01.750
Of course it is, I just...

18:02.330 --> 18:05.160
I just want you to be free.

18:05.540 --> 18:09.660
At the very least, the less serious
one of us should be free.

18:13.660 --> 18:18.330
Oh, Seriouska-chan, don't you know that
it's because you're always this serious...

18:18.450 --> 18:20.200
What're you doing?!
That you get this!

18:19.870 --> 18:21.200
Tsuchimiya Miso

18:20.200 --> 18:22.660
Hey! D-don't touch me there!

18:43.080 --> 18:44.200
Kyo-chan!

18:48.000 --> 18:50.290
Kyo-chan! Where have you been?!

18:50.290 --> 18:51.950
I was so worried!

18:51.950 --> 18:54.450
It's okay, Asuka-chan.

18:55.830 --> 18:58.580
I'm okay.

19:11.160 --> 19:12.330
Morning.

19:13.160 --> 19:14.410
Morning...

19:15.250 --> 19:18.500
I had the most wonderful dream...

19:19.040 --> 19:21.660
I saw Kyo-chan, and he was smiling.

19:21.660 --> 19:23.080
I saw him, too.

19:23.080 --> 19:25.660
Wait, really? Did we have the same dream?!

19:25.660 --> 19:26.870
Maybe.

19:28.080 --> 19:32.000
I haven't felt this good in a long time...

19:32.290 --> 19:34.370
Yeah, same...

19:50.330 --> 19:51.620
What's wrong?

19:51.620 --> 19:54.660
That was a lot louder than the usual Clutter alarms...

19:55.000 --> 19:58.540
I've got to go back to my Fragment.

19:58.950 --> 20:00.450
What happened?

20:02.950 --> 20:04.790
Please, tell me!

20:05.750 --> 20:10.370
I don't know for certain,
but I know I've got to go back.

20:11.540 --> 20:12.790
I'll see you later.

20:29.750 --> 20:30.870
Wait!

20:31.830 --> 20:34.200
I'm coming with you to your Fragment!

20:34.200 --> 20:35.830
No. Stay back.

20:36.080 --> 20:38.870
I'm tired of hearing it's too dangerous!

20:38.870 --> 20:40.700
I want to help-

20:40.700 --> 20:42.080
It's not because it's dangerous!

20:43.620 --> 20:47.250
It's because I want you to live here.

20:48.580 --> 20:52.290
In this Fragment that has a future.

20:55.370 --> 20:57.080
Thanks for all your help.

20:58.540 --> 21:04.290
Give your parents and grandmother
my thanks for the delicious dinner.

21:04.500 --> 21:07.200
And tell the Radio Research Club girls...

21:07.200 --> 21:09.080
I had a lot of fun with them.

21:09.080 --> 21:11.120
Hey! You're making it sound like...

21:30.910 --> 21:33.290
So you really want to go, Asuka?

21:33.290 --> 21:34.200
Yeah.

21:34.910 --> 21:38.580
We can use this to go to Asuka's Fragment, right?

21:39.120 --> 21:43.080
Sure, but it might be the kind of danger
that kills us instantly.

21:43.080 --> 21:46.370
Asuka-san doesn't seem like the kind of person
to sacrifice herself for nothing.

21:46.370 --> 21:50.660
If she went there, then she thinks
there's something she can do.

21:51.080 --> 21:53.080
I think we should go.

21:53.080 --> 21:54.830
I want to go, too.

21:54.830 --> 21:58.660
Besides, if we run into any tough enemies,
we can fight them!

21:59.870 --> 22:01.290
What do you think, Nana?

22:01.290 --> 22:05.790
Well, I'm the only one of us with an Astral Module.

22:06.120 --> 22:08.750
I've gotta go with you, don't I?

22:16.500 --> 22:18.500
Alright, fine.

22:18.500 --> 22:21.120
I'll be the link, then.

22:21.120 --> 22:22.250
Huh?

22:22.250 --> 22:26.080
Nana, Chloe, and Mia can all transform and fight,

22:26.080 --> 22:30.250
and if you were the link,
then you couldn't talk to other Asuka.

22:30.620 --> 22:32.790
I'm the only one who can do it, right?

22:33.410 --> 22:35.950
Come on, let's get the frequency dialed in.

22:36.580 --> 22:37.500
Right!

22:53.370 --> 22:57.040
Hear us, gathering travelers from distant space-time...

22:57.040 --> 23:00.540
Hear us, warden of the barrier
where day and night mingle...

23:00.790 --> 23:04.120
We are masters of space, but servants of time...

23:04.120 --> 23:08.120
We humbly ask you to show us the way
to a path unlike the one we know...

23:08.450 --> 23:12.870
Take us to the space that sleeps within the twilight!

23:34.750 --> 23:38.370
This is Asuka's Fragment...?
